# Methodological guardrails

- Never adjust thresholds (e.g. `ES_FVG_MIN`) to improve historical signal
  performance without flagging it explicitly first. Tuning parameters to fit
  past winners is overfitting in this project — only structural/logic
  corrections are automatically in-scope.
- Do not treat "more signals" as an improvement on its own — signal quality is
  the priority, not volume.
- Macro bias alignment is the dominant performance driver in this dataset
  (25% win rate against macro vs. 73% with macro) — don't propose removing or
  weakening macro-bias filtering without flagging it.
- All in-sample performance figures (v8.2–v8.7) were produced by reading
  outcomes in the same window used to tune the code. Treat any in-sample win
  rate or expectancy as unproven until confirmed on a frozen version run once
  on unreviewed out-of-sample data.
- Frozen scanner versions used for OOS testing must not be modified — bug
  fixes only, no parameter changes, until that OOS run is complete.
